# B-LANGSTON-CONTEXT P-7 — rotation for the recall usage log.
# Matched DELIBERATELY to /etc/logrotate.d/langston-instructions-loaded, its sibling
# instrument, so the two observability logs age the same way rather than each carrying
# a different half-remembered policy.
# ⛔ IT EXISTS BECAUSE THIS BATCH IS ABOUT UNBOUNDED APPEND-ONLY GROWTH. Shipping a new
#    append-only artifact with no eviction rule would rebuild, in the instrument, the
#    exact failure the batch was opened to fix.
# copytruncate: the writer opens and closes per row, so `create` would also work — but
#    copytruncate preserves the inode and therefore the langston:langston ownership.
# ⛔⛔ `su` IS LOAD-BEARING, NOT BOILERPLATE — MEASURED 2026-09-05. Without it logrotate
#    REFUSES this file outright: "parent directory has insecure permissions". The usage
#    directory is created by the tool under langston's umask, so it is group-writable,
#    and logrotate will not rotate into a directory it does not consider safe.
# ★ IT FAILED SILENTLY IN THE SENSE THAT MATTERS: the config was valid, the file was
#    installed, and NOTHING would ever have rotated. A rotation rule that never runs
#    reads as coverage and provides none. Caught only by FORCING a rotation and looking
#    at the result, not by installing the config and assuming.
/opt/langston-memory/usage/recall-usage.jsonl {
    su langston langston
    weekly
    rotate 8
    compress
    notifempty
    copytruncate
}

# The other two P-7/P-5 logs. Same policy, same `su` reasoning — all three live in the
# same group-writable directory, so all three need it.
# ⛔ ADDED IN THE SAME BREATH AS THE INSTRUMENTS THEMSELVES, deliberately: this batch
#    exists because an append-only artifact grew unwatched. Shipping three new
#    append-only artifacts without eviction would be the same mistake, three times.
/opt/langston-memory/usage/load-canary.jsonl
/opt/langston-memory/usage/size-watch.jsonl
/opt/langston-memory/usage/selfmemory-backup.jsonl {
    su langston langston
    weekly
    rotate 8
    compress
    notifempty
    copytruncate
}
